abstract: "A red/blue colouring of the complete graph on 1660 vertices with no monochromatic K_12, so R(12,12) ≥ 1661. It consists of the Mathon–Shearer colouring M(797) with 21 vertices removed, and 85 core vertices, each a copy of a removed vertex or constant on the rest of M(797). The removed vertices contain two antipodal pairs of M(797). Checked by two independent exhaustive computer searches and by a clone-projection argument with an antipodal rule, and proved in Lean 4 with Mathlib; the compiled proof was also accepted by leanchecker and by the independent kernel nanoda. The work was done with Claude (Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic); see the README."
keywords:
  - Ramsey numbers
  - lower bounds
  - Lean
